// The Safety Knowledge Base: 255 rules in eight databases, as facts.
//
// Generated once on 2026-10-31 from skb/rules/*.json, which `--emit-skb` wrote
// from the tables then in prototype/src/skb.rs. From here on this file is the
// statement: `builtin_rules()` reads it, and skb/ is generated from that.
//
// These rules are knowledge. No component executes one: `codegen_bridge` keeps
// their descriptions as strings and `rmi_ontology_adapter` searches them. So
// `unenforced_rule` exempts SafetyRule, and no `enforced_by` is stated here.
//
// A rule is one `safety_rule` row: id, database, category, severity,
// description, rationale, fix confidence. `rule_fix` is its auto-fix template,
// if it has one. `rule_tag` gives each tag its position, because the order of
// a rule's tags is part of the policy digest. Rules are in id order within a
// database; order in this file does not matter.

